AU  - Du, Wenjiao
AU  - Ye, Qizheng
AU  - Yuan, Zhe
AU  - Li, Chenmeng
T2  - Gaoya Dianqi High Voltage Apparatus
AB  - The temperature measurement technology based on light radiation generally works in the infrared band with strong thermal radiation. Although the temperature measurement technology based on light reflection can work in the visible band, yet the present application conditions are limited to the normal incident single wavelength visible light source in the dark environment, and it is difficult for power equipment to use this technology when working under the sunshine. In this paper, through digital image processing technology and machine learning method, the thermally modulated light reflection technology is extended to the case without needing normal incidence and fixed light source, and the identification of surface temperature rise of electrical fitting at normal temperature is achieved by using sunlight.In the sunlight, we used three kinds of mobile phones to take photos and established 4 500 image libraries of one kind of fitting for 110 kV transmission line with different sunlight environments (there are three kinds of sunlight illumination at each temperature), and 1 500 image libraries of each of three kinds of fittings (one kind of sunlight illumination at each temperature), extracted the three primary colours gray frequency distribution (RGB-GLH) of each photo as the feature quantity, and established the identification model of surface temperature through such four machine learning methods as support vector machine, decision tree method, gradient lifting method and k-nearest neighbor method. The cross-validation results show that the k-nearest neighbor method is optimal, and the mean absolute error is suitable for identifying the temperature rise of faults of general fitting. Based on the electromagnetic characteristics of materials and in accordance with the reflection law of electromagnetic wave, the principle of thermal modulated light reflection temperature rise identification technology in sunlight and the basis of using machine learning method to process big data matrix are also discussed.
