T2  - 2nd International Conference on Machine Learning and Autonomous Systems Icmlas 2025 Proceedings
AB  - The integration of digital technology in healthcare has been greatly facilitated by the internet. It has made access to vital data quite easy, with which solutions created help in improving patient outcomes. This leads to an improvement in patient care and medical procedures. Vigilance is required to avoid the dissemination of information that may be incorrect or dangerous, and thus harm patients and healthcare providers alike. The amount of patient-generated data involved is huge, and this has become quite central to the drug recommendation system in the healthcare industry. It is envisioned that medication recommendations by these systems are highly precise to increase efficacy and accuracy of treatment. Using Natural Language Processing tools, the suggested approach will make a prediction about the best drug, using ratings and reviews made by the patients. It would be advisable to apply some NLP approaches to the input provided by the patient to extract some useful insights and information that might help in prescription decisions. Examples of some machine learning methods applied for enhancing accuracy and dependability of such drug recommendations include the XGBoost classifier and LightGBM model. These algorithms further process and analyse data to bring out the relationships and patterns not otherwise evident. They therefore provide crucial help toward the formation and establishment of an effective or reliable drug-related recommendation system and greatly improved the treatment of patients.
